{
  "tema": 5256,
  "slug": "busque",
  "titulo": "-car verbs in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Busqué mis llaves; él buscó la tabla.",
  "foto": "t07.jpg",
  "regla": "In the preterite, -ar verbs ending in -car change c to qu in the yo form only (busqué, saqué, toqué) to keep the hard k sound. All other forms are regular: buscaste, buscó.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs ending in **-car** are regular -ar verbs in the preterite, with **one spelling change**: in **yo**, the **c** becomes **qu**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Why? **ce** sounds like _se_. To keep the hard _k_ sound before **é**, Spanish writes **qué**: **busqué**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "buscar",
            "sacar",
            "tocar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "busqué",
              "saqué",
              "toqué"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "buscaste",
              "sacaste",
              "tocaste"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "buscó",
              "sacó",
              "tocó"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "buscamos",
              "sacamos",
              "tocamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "buscaron",
              "sacaron",
              "tocaron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Common ones: **buscar**, **sacar**, **tocar**, **practicar**, **explicar**, **marcar**, **pescar**, **secar**, **chocar**, **colocar**, **indicar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Keep the **accent**: **busqué** (preterite). Without it, **busque** is a different form (subjunctive)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the sound never changes; only the spelling does. Say it first, then write the letters that make that sound."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
